 \label{cos-lemma}
Let us fix any $\varrho \in \mathbb N$ whose binary digits are $\{\mathtt d_{\ell}(\varrho): \ell \geq 0\}$: 
\begin{equation} \label{rho-expansion}   
\varrho = \sum_{\ell \geq 0} \mathtt d_\ell(\varrho) 2^{\ell}, \quad \mathtt d_{\ell}(\cdot) \in \{0,1\}. 
\end{equation} 
Assume there exists an index $k \in \mathbb N$ such that $ \bigl(\mathtt d_{k-1}(\varrho), \mathtt d_k(\varrho) \bigr) \ne (0,0)$ or $(1,1)$. Then  
\begin{equation} \label{cos-small}
\bigl| \cos \bigl(\pi \varrho 2^{-k-1}\bigr) \bigr| = \Bigl| \frac{1}{2} \Bigl(1 + e(\varrho 2^{-k-1})\Bigr) \Bigr| \leq \cos \Bigl(\frac{\pi}{4}\Bigr) = \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}<1.   
\end{equation}

\begin{equation} \label{rho-expansion}   
\varrho = \sum_{\ell \geq 0} \mathtt d_\ell(\varrho) 2^{\ell}, \quad \mathtt d_{\ell}(\cdot) \in \{0,1\}. 
